Facts from other projects
-------------------------

- python-miio (github.com/rytilahti/python-miio, GPL-3.0): the miIO
  packet and the method sets of the legacy models the simulator answers
  (facts only; no code was taken).
- Xiaomi-cloud-tokens-extractor
  (github.com/PiotrMachowski/Xiaomi-cloud-tokens-extractor; MIT,
  Copyright (c) 2020 Piotr Machowski): the Mi account endpoints the
  simulated account answers (facts only).
- The Yeelight Inter-Operation Specification: that a Yeelight refuses
  changes while off.
- miot-spec.org: the format the simulated specification service serves.

Interop tests (interop/, a separate test-only module)
-----------------------------------------------------

interop/peer/Dockerfile downloads python-miio (GPL-3.0) at a fixed
commit and installs it, with its dependencies, into a python:3.12-slim
image at test time, to run its client; nothing of python-miio is copied
into this repository, and it is not linked with this module.
interop/peer/client.py is our own script that calls python-miio.

